s, or a surge of Democratic outside spending, would signal the race is tightening.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Newest usable poll is 49 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Open seat: Dusty Johnson (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "South Dakota's at-large House seat is open after Dusty Johnson retired to run for governor, but the district's R+15 partisan lean keeps the seat firmly in Republican territory. Former attorney general Marty Jackley won the Republican primary and enters the general election with a clear financial edge, having raised about $1.7 million and holding roughly $1.2 million on hand. Democrat Nikki Gronli has raised about $387,000 with limited cash remaining.\n\nThe only recent poll, conducted for a Democratic sponsor in late August, showed Jackley ahead 47 to 43 among likely voters. Prediction markets price the Republican at about 95 percent. The forecast expects a Republican win by roughly fourteen points, with the open-seat dynamic and thin polling leaving modest room for a closer finish.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0322, "margin": -15.31}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.035, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0242, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0439, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0257, "margin": -15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0188, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0357, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0228, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0239, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.019, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.015, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0299, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0301, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0189, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.036, "ma